SupraLINUX ksshaskpass

Official signed source remains unchanged. Preserve the Ubuntu epoch, openssh
dependency, ssh-askpass alternatives priority/manpage slave, and documentation.
Upstream now uses QtKeychain rather than linking directly to KWallet. Required
Frameworks inputs are frozen; Qt and QtKeychain come from Ubuntu.

The private offscreen fixture is built against Ubuntu Qt before upgrade. It
interposes only Qt dialog/event-loop entrypoints to schedule public widget input
and button clicks, then calls the original event loops and application result
handling. Password masking, cancellation and OpenSSH confirm/none prompt modes
must match real Ubuntu behavior. No return result or keychain data is fabricated.
The prompts never request wallet lookup or storage. D-Bus, HOME/XDG directories
and subprocess groups are private; input/output is synthetic. Consumer tests
rebuild the fixture after upgrade. Local Ubuntu preparation does not certify the
candidate; real KDE/SSH/keychain session integration remains a separate gate.
